  "novel_mechanics_found": "L5's small black/yellow diamond is not decorative: it is the selected-state rendering of a carrier handle, while green/yellow diamonds are unselected handles. The board has a two-handle carrier and a three-handle carrier; overlapping black-backed colored cargo attaches it to the carrier, and overlapping another cargo stacks/fuses the payload. A click inside a different handle diamond silently switches carrier/handle control. Cargo/socket contact is highly alignment-sensitive, several same-color-looking and cross-color-looking dotted glyphs are decoys or blockers, and the hard meter allows exactly 60 level actions before the next action causes GAME_OVER.",
  "narrative": "Fresh-replayed the 141-action banked prefix and confirmed frame.levels_completed reached 4 before exploration. Spent eight live L5 attempts mapping every visible cargo, socket, handle, and both carriers; recovered and optimized the prior near-route to an exact 60-click candidate, but no attempt advanced the frame beyond level 4. The final candidate replayed deterministically through the full meter and still left levels_completed at 4. Stopped at 583 total env.step calls: the remaining 117 calls were insufficient for the mandatory 141-call fresh reproduction gate, so no new win is claimed and reproduction_verified is false.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The 141-action prefix was replayed from a fresh env.reset() and manually observed at levels_completed=4 before exploration.",
    "L5 has a hard 60-action meter. Rejected clicks, selection clicks, and apparent no-ops consume it; the action after depletion produces GAME_OVER.",
    "The black/yellow diamond is a selected handle, not a separate cargo or decorative glyph. Green/yellow diamonds are unselected handles.",
    "Clicking any cell inside another handle's diamond can silently switch selection, including switching onto the other carrier during a geometrically valid route.",
    "The upper carrier has two handles and the lower carrier has three; moving cargo with the wrong carrier can produce convincing but non-winning alignments.",
    "A carrier picks up black-backed colored cargo on overlap, and a second cargo can visibly join the moving payload.",
    "Dotted sockets and solid payloads can occlude one another; temporary palette-count drops while overlapped are not evidence of delivery. Move away and re-read the frame before concluding that dots or cargo were consumed.",
    "Several dotted glyphs share one payload color or visually suggest a complementary mapping but are real blockers/decoys; neither simple same-color matching nor the tested cross-color mapping produced an L5 win.",
    "GameAction.RESET restores L5 while preserving levels_completed; reset actions and exploratory tails are intentionally absent from action_sequence."
  ],
